om 1951 to 2025 shows September to October and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 35 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025, August to September ran 55% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 50% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2001, and grids 19417 and 19717 got just 59% of normal that year.</p>"}
